    "long_instructions": "This is Lesson 8, Level 2 (Nearest Neighbors Classification), right after Level 1 shows the initial plot and prediction. The real circulate note here: check whether students connect changing a feature's value to the prediction actually changing, specifically, prompt them to notice how moving Today toward one group of points changes which neighbors end up closest.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n- Edit the values of the delivery date’s features.\r\n- Run your program again.\r\n- Pay attention to how the prediction changes. You’ll answer a question about this later.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Reflection:** If a student changes a feature's value but the prediction stays exactly the same, is that a sign something's wrong, or expected behavior? What would you want them to notice about where \"Today\" sits relative to its neighbors in either case?\r\n",
